---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="What the Weekend Engineering Digest is, how items get picked, and who writes it."
>
  <h1>About</h1>

  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      A weekly roundup of what engineering teams actually published — distributed systems,
      architecture, AI infrastructure and agents, platform and reliability engineering. Four to six
      items, each with a short summary of the engineering insight and why it matters. About five
      minutes to read.
    </p>

    <h2>How items get picked</h2>
    <p>
      Sourced from primary engineering blogs rather than aggregators: Netflix, Stripe, Cloudflare,
      Meta, GitHub, Uber, Discord, and others, plus AI-engineering writing and general architecture
      news. The filter is concrete engineering substance — a measured tradeoff, a design constraint,
      a number someone had to defend. Vendor announcements and listicles don't make it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Everything links to the original post. The summaries are commentary meant to help you decide
      what's worth your time; the source is always where the real detail lives.
    </p>

    <h2>Who writes it</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="https://pradnya.dev/">Pradnya Wakchaure</a>, a software engineer in New York working
      on distributed systems and AI tooling. Opinions here are hers alone and not those of any
      employer.
    </p>

    <h2>Subscribing</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="/rss.xml">RSS</a> for now. An email edition will follow.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
